  "note": "SAY YOUR DAY — Reza, 2026-10-12: 'if I could just talk about my day or feel like I am able to speak more about my day I might feel good … the biggest demotivating is my Preply class when I can't have a simple conversation.' First-person sentences about HIS actual day (Fajr, the train, the office, the children, the evening that is his, the weekend, the Sunday lesson), ≤ 7 words, present and past, plus the questions she is likely to ask. The daily block 'Say your day' draws from these through the Free-try engine; the ones he has said and been understood become his Sunday script. Hand-checked. Fields: moment (morning|commute|work|evening|yesterday|weekend|smalltalk|her), who (me|her), swap = what to change to make it his own.",
  "sentences": [
    { "id": "md:0", "moment": "morning", "who": "me", "ar": "أَسْتَيْقِظُ قَبْلَ الفَجْرِ.", "en": "I wake up before Fajr.", "tr": "astayqiẓu qabla l-fajr", "swap": "before → after; Fajr → seven" },
